-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6e70d3f677cfec4029edbada88fe4f1e88cd4732","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6e70d3f677cfec4029edbada88fe4f1e88cd4732","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/6e70d3f677cfec4029edbada88fe4f1e88cd4732"}]},{"sha":"6e70d3f677cfec4029edbada88fe4f1e88cd4732","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDZlNzBkM2Y2NzdjZmVjNDAyOWVkYmFkYTg4ZmU0ZjFlODhjZDQ3MzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-28T06:41:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T06:41:47Z"},"message":"fix(plugin): delegate compaction to OpenClaw runtime SDK to unwedge over-budget groups (CAURA-000) (#234)\n\n## Summary\n\n**Urgent hotfix for v2.6.3 regression.** Customer escalation 2026-05-26:\nWhatsApp group sessions stuck running, looping on `memclaw_keystones`\ntool calls without finalizing, emitting `Skipping auto-reply: ...\nfinal-only` warnings. Group contexts reported over budget at 312k/272k\nand 292k/272k tokens via `openclaw status`. Direct chats with the same\nagent worked normally.\n\n**Root cause:** `MemClawContextEngine.info.ownsCompaction = true` told\nOpenClaw we owned compaction, but `compact()` returned `undefined` — not\na valid `CompactResult` per OpenClaw 2026.5.4\n`plugin-sdk/src/context-engine/types.d.ts`. Over-budget sessions\ndelegated to us, got nothing back, never shrank. Direct chats stayed\nunder budget so the latent bug never surfaced; group chats accumulate\ntranscript across participants and hit the wedge first.\n\n**Fix:** stay `ownsCompaction: true` (truthful) and have `compact()`\nactually do its job by delegating to `delegateCompactionToRuntime` from\n`openclaw/plugin-sdk` — the same helper the legacy engine uses\ninternally. Required a runtime SDK-discovery bridge\n(`openclaw-sdk-bridge.ts`) because OpenClaw's plugin loader routes `.js`\nfiles through native Node import, which bypasses the alias-map that\nwould normally resolve the bare-spec import. Plus a defensive pre-check\nthat returns a structured `CompactResult` fallback when\n`sessionId`/`sessionFile` are missing, blocking degenerate calls from\nreaching `compactEmbeddedPiSessionDirect` (which we observed can crash\nthe gateway with synthetic params).\n\nNote: I considered the simpler `ownsCompaction: false` change first. Per\nOpenClaw docs (`docs/concepts/context-engine.md:241`), `false` does NOT\nauto-fall-back to legacy compaction — it just disables compaction\nentirely. So we have to delegate explicitly to fulfill the contract.\n\n## Files changed\n\n- **`plugin/src/openclaw-sdk-bridge.ts`** (new, 203 lines): runtime SDK\ndiscovery via `process.argv[1]` walk → first `package.json` with `name:\n\"openclaw\"` → absolute-path dynamic import of\n`dist/plugin-sdk/index.js`. Structurally-typed surface, no build-time\ndep on `openclaw`. Cached resolver state for the process lifetime.\n`_resetSdkBridgeCache()` exposed for tests.\n- **`plugin/src/context-engine.ts`**:\n- `info.ownsCompaction` stays `true`; comment block expanded to document\nwhy and warn against flipping (per the OpenClaw docs).\n- `compact()` rewritten with three responsibilities: persist OpenClaw's\npre-computed summary as a MemClaw `auto-compaction` episode (preserved);\ndefensive guard for missing `sessionId`/`sessionFile`; delegate to the\nSDK helper via the bridge. Pass the runtime's `CompactResult` through\nverbatim. Structured fallback on any internal failure.\n  - File-level docstring updated.\n- **`plugin/src/runtime-contract.test.ts`** (179 new lines): 9 new tests\ncovering `ownsCompaction === true` invariant, bridge null-safety in test\nenvs, bridge cache idempotency, `compact()` always returns CompactResult\nshape (regression guard from v2.6.3's `undefined`), the defensive guards\nfor missing `sessionId`/`sessionFile`.\n- `plugin/package.json` + `plugin/openclaw.plugin.json` +\n`plugin/src/version.ts` (auto-regen): 2.6.3 → 2.6.4.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm test` in `plugin/` — **259/259 pass** (250 prior + 9 new\ncompaction-bridge tests).\n- [x] `npx tsc --noEmit` clean.\n- [x] **Wet-test on GCE VM** (`openclaw-test-ran`) with **OpenClaw\n2026.5.4** + v2.6.4 build (probe-E):\n- Boot: `[memclaw] BOOT: plugin v2.6.4, 11 tools registered, node\n22.22.1`; `ContextEngine 'memclaw' registered`; zero `assemble failed`\nlines; zero warnings.\n- Bridge resolves SDK from real plugin loader context: `sdk=object,\ndelegate=function`.\n  - `info.ownsCompaction=true, id=memclaw`.\n- `compact({})`, `compact({sessionId, sessionFile: \"\"})`,\n`compact({summary})` all return structured `CompactResult` via the\ndefensive guard — no hang, no crash, no thrown error.\n- `assemble({...})` returns `messages: array, estimatedTokens: 152,\nsystemPromptAddition.length: 605` — unchanged from v2.6.3.\n- [ ] **Pending customer verification post-2.6.4 publish**: WhatsApp\ngroup session no longer wedges on over-budget; `<keystone_rules>` block\nstill appears in system prompt; assemble + compaction both function\nend-to-end.\n\n## Customer mitigation (immediate, no code push needed)\n\nFor customers stuck on v2.6.3, regress the slot until v2.6.4 is\npublished:\n\n```bash\nsudo cp ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json.v263-broken\npython3 -c \"import json;p='/home/'+__import__('os').getenv('USER')+'/.openclaw/openclaw.json';c=json.load(open(p));c['plugins']['slots'].pop('contextEngine',None);json.dump(c,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\"\necho \"MEMCLAW_AUTO_FIX_CONFIG=false\" >> ~/.openclaw/plugins/memclaw/.env\nsudo systemctl restart openclaw\n```\n\nThis regresses in-prompt keystone injection (the `memclaw_keystones`\ntool call surface stays functional) but unwedges over-budget sessions\nimmediately. After 2.6.4 lands, customers remove the `.env` line +\ndelete the slot removal, restart — the upgrade re-claims the slot and\nkeystone injection resumes with proper compaction delegation.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: ran-taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7688ecdbd2f9759338c183f670f9add24e7cfa4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/7688ecdbd2f9759338c183f670f9add24e7cfa4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/6e70d3f677cfec4029edbada88fe4f1e88cd4732","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqF+OrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/5IQAGyZeEtMDZSVBkEDLCX7oOFJ\nwk2GPyLSPziEtLDRfcJGeqkgE8/oo+Ua+Jk5aiBpdL1VjDnf1oOu93/t0q1hfutU\n5PkQICGwNMOUYjpIJZrTIuXQ/B0lltb63LGDLU3vY/oWal9y58RDza/32XtELBJl\nDlYyOhmN3N7ySm1AB54i/ckinsuxs5dTTLO+JEsdPd9s8QwAUYqsrV3GgADtY/Gv\nCDj+cMDK4IvbIiB36FnTnz/y4ujWULtbBO+CbUsaUkuRVOZsFZtouAckJ1RP+bcS\nB2g1y8SaPOFMtzSkIfVBRukliZ8QWl5FB57EitROr22vOCmQXZb/LRQUHGhxYfd5\ndD8g/1yLAALl9DUXgfDnii3BvKJjRkBghFn2TboCXVGH2+R2/5g/RNCV5/K7THOG\n4LsuaCCXnO3jr7I+0hSKnPOVZY9O2s9fkTthqx/bTR3+LNbROUjcsdshNdmeQdii\nFerlp0c1RjfDrNrmDjbdKRlUrLIjcVWRSnOtRYqfRUpHVMp6YR2apKEDGpbIJpYv\nqWpPAUs5DCJH5GV/3hM/shZDVAcTxm6tJCSeg5gjdw1NThx3LzqFZY5nOUgW6apW\nsJykANq4CG4O4w4sEujwhdUX/Ra3n3g5o+DfdprtMgYISAtp9A6DUFoqHs+tUfjB\nZPUWtyoFtkD0FYlYxlM9\n=vO64\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7688ecdbd2f9759338c183f670f9add24e7cfa4a\nparent f5668f6d0e99ee4f3d4612c8dbdafcaff2a8bb13\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1779950507 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779950507 +0300\n\nfix(plugin): delegate compaction to OpenClaw runtime SDK to unwedge over-budget groups (CAURA-000) (#234)\n\n## Summary\n\n**Urgent hotfix for v2.6.3 regression.** Customer escalation 2026-05-26:\nWhatsApp group sessions stuck running, looping on `memclaw_keystones`\ntool calls without finalizing, emitting `Skipping auto-reply: ...\nfinal-only` warnings. Group contexts reported over budget at 312k/272k\nand 292k/272k tokens via `openclaw status`. Direct chats with the same\nagent worked normally.\n\n**Root cause:** `MemClawContextEngine.info.ownsCompaction = true` told\nOpenClaw we owned compaction, but `compact()` returned `undefined` — not\na valid `CompactResult` per OpenClaw 2026.5.4\n`plugin-sdk/src/context-engine/types.d.ts`. Over-budget sessions\ndelegated to us, got nothing back, never shrank. Direct chats stayed\nunder budget so the latent bug never surfaced; group chats accumulate\ntranscript across participants and hit the wedge first.\n\n**Fix:** stay `ownsCompaction: true` (truthful) and have `compact()`\nactually do its job by delegating to `delegateCompactionToRuntime` from\n`openclaw/plugin-sdk` — the same helper the legacy engine uses\ninternally. Required a runtime SDK-discovery bridge\n(`openclaw-sdk-bridge.ts`) because OpenClaw's plugin loader routes `.js`\nfiles through native Node import, which bypasses the alias-map that\nwould normally resolve the bare-spec import. Plus a defensive pre-check\nthat returns a structured `CompactResult` fallback when\n`sessionId`/`sessionFile` are missing, blocking degenerate calls from\nreaching `compactEmbeddedPiSessionDirect` (which we observed can crash\nthe gateway with synthetic params).\n\nNote: I considered the simpler `ownsCompaction: false` change first. Per\nOpenClaw docs (`docs/concepts/context-engine.md:241`), `false` does NOT\nauto-fall-back to legacy compaction — it just disables compaction\nentirely. So we have to delegate explicitly to fulfill the contract.\n\n## Files changed\n\n- **`plugin/src/openclaw-sdk-bridge.ts`** (new, 203 lines): runtime SDK\ndiscovery via `process.argv[1]` walk → first `package.json` with `name:\n\"openclaw\"` → absolute-path dynamic import of\n`dist/plugin-sdk/index.js`. Structurally-typed surface, no build-time\ndep on `openclaw`. Cached resolver state for the process lifetime.\n`_resetSdkBridgeCache()` exposed for tests.\n- **`plugin/src/context-engine.ts`**:\n- `info.ownsCompaction` stays `true`; comment block expanded to document\nwhy and warn against flipping (per the OpenClaw docs).\n- `compact()` rewritten with three responsibilities: persist OpenClaw's\npre-computed summary as a MemClaw `auto-compaction` episode (preserved);\ndefensive guard for missing `sessionId`/`sessionFile`; delegate to the\nSDK helper via the bridge. Pass the runtime's `CompactResult` through\nverbatim. Structured fallback on any internal failure.\n  - File-level docstring updated.\n- **`plugin/src/runtime-contract.test.ts`** (179 new lines): 9 new tests\ncovering `ownsCompaction === true` invariant, bridge null-safety in test\nenvs, bridge cache idempotency, `compact()` always returns CompactResult\nshape (regression guard from v2.6.3's `undefined`), the defensive guards\nfor missing `sessionId`/`sessionFile`.\n- `plugin/package.json` + `plugin/openclaw.plugin.json` +\n`plugin/src/version.ts` (auto-regen): 2.6.3 → 2.6.4.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm test` in `plugin/` — **259/259 pass** (250 prior + 9 new\ncompaction-bridge tests).\n- [x] `npx tsc --noEmit` clean.\n- [x] **Wet-test on GCE VM** (`openclaw-test-ran`) with **OpenClaw\n2026.5.4** + v2.6.4 build (probe-E):\n- Boot: `[memclaw] BOOT: plugin v2.6.4, 11 tools registered, node\n22.22.1`; `ContextEngine 'memclaw' registered`; zero `assemble failed`\nlines; zero warnings.\n- Bridge resolves SDK from real plugin loader context: `sdk=object,\ndelegate=function`.\n  - `info.ownsCompaction=true, id=memclaw`.\n- `compact({})`, `compact({sessionId, sessionFile: \"\"})`,\n`compact({summary})` all return structured `CompactResult` via the\ndefensive guard — no hang, no crash, no thrown error.\n- `assemble({...})` returns `messages: array, estimatedTokens: 152,\nsystemPromptAddition.length: 605` — unchanged from v2.6.3.\n- [ ] **Pending customer verification post-2.6.4 publish**: WhatsApp\ngroup session no longer wedges on over-budget; `<keystone_rules>` block\nstill appears in system prompt; assemble + compaction both function\nend-to-end.\n\n## Customer mitigation (immediate, no code push needed)\n\nFor customers stuck on v2.6.3, regress the slot until v2.6.4 is\npublished:\n\n```bash\nsudo cp ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json.v263-broken\npython3 -c \"import json;p='/home/'+__import__('os').getenv('USER')+'/.openclaw/openclaw.json';c=json.load(open(p));c['plugins']['slots'].pop('contextEngine',None);json.dump(c,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\"\necho \"MEMCLAW_AUTO_FIX_CONFIG=false\" >> ~/.openclaw/plugins/memclaw/.env\nsudo systemctl restart openclaw\n```\n\nThis regresses in-prompt keystone injection (the `memclaw_keystones`\ntool call surface stays functional) but unwedges over-budget sessions\nimmediately. After 2.6.4 lands, customers remove the `.env` line +\ndelete the slot removal, restart — the upgrade re-claims the slot and\nkeystone injection resumes with proper compaction delegation.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: ran-taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-28T06:41:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6e70d3f677cfec4029edbada88fe4f1e88cd4732","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/6e70d3f677cfec4029edbada88fe4f1e88cd4732","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6e70d3f677cfec4029edbada88fe4f1e88cd4732/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f5668f6d0e99ee4f3d4612c8dbdafcaff2a8bb13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f5668f6d0e99ee4f3d4612c8dbdafcaff2a8bb13","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f5668f6d0e99ee4f3d4612c8dbdafcaff2a8bb13"}]},{"sha":"f5668f6d0e99ee4f3d4612c8dbdafcaff2a8bb13","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGY1NjY4ZjZkMGU5OWVlNGYzZDQ2MTJjOGRiZGFmY2FmZjJhOGJiMTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-28T06:21:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T06:21:01Z"},"message":"fix(version-compat): bump MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION to 2.6.4 (#242)\n\nCompanion PR to #234 (urgent v2.6.3 group-chat compaction-wedge hotfix).\n\nWithout this bump, v2.6.3 nodes wouldn't auto-deploy to v2.6.4 — the\nheartbeat handler gates auto-deploy on `plugin_version <\nMIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION`. With the previous floor of 2.6.3,\nexisting 2.6.3 nodes sit at the threshold and the deploy command never\nfires.\n\nSame release-process gap PRs #204 (2.5.0 → 2.6.2) and #226 (2.6.2 →\n2.6.3) closed.\n\n## Merge order\nShould be merged **after** PR #234 lands (so the new plugin code is on\nmain when this bump tells the server to push it).\n\n## Follow-up\nHave release-please auto-sync this constant from plugin/package.json so\nwe don't need a manual companion PR per plugin release. Tracked\nseparately.\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"d8830adee5baa50596b8bf00961c5a06cde582fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/d8830adee5baa50596b8bf00961c5a06cde582fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/f5668f6d0e99ee4f3d4612c8dbdafcaff2a8bb13","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqF97NCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACKMQAKMZz6FwcU3Tptr/96qGhbtN\nYOLPXd3u9qssC29ViKxtbSWGQGC2zoWo8DAjtCTxWXJhH0sqg2xShomdo3Kh1Fc2\nbwtjJaBvKmDbC4C03Mj5lYrFOAzcvV4YdAInxOfcaMUaEKMWMcoPaznXhZ0noYNN\ngMb9WaZ0gXMzzPzL4tXSynPoW4ZpoK/qDjA3GXksvHfQniuEB0KhJAJyngJwQyWa\nGbMuYcTdS+u4M7c+RReN17eBW4J268jU7R1SkQAtYynlYwpQ8WjWIaON4ruphyaC\nUsqoPqTVJFi4ywtIwc04a/rO5XiL+K78FtoWFfc3zT/uJpK1GAlJCokYqxYc+6D5\n0y1ActJQa5AiE0IDE0qMnuD5UoVHO1Rke5hJIpjCZ3GmUh1bcHgSFwWXtjp8nqh7\nJKtczwyIIfq+VVZ4HSZIIMfIPKOBpaiE1Z1v98og2+vWloCT/WEWsIrbNNeA4PIh\nMmB0ssrWQnFvaDwozgRTXLrgapQgPHa0Stq8Jh2jPaUSK1Ysq7LscMDKytxhrHSP\njG7z8qtRK4vH+xQECwGybCJyH0P7HpFNz/wTzttsG1+PIpRR7TA4yR5+gsv5kr4J\nFlCwNFae7TJnk+/zYGE2wIMBN6c3HMwrT4R66od4WSNHHbzmUSRjB/fjg2rO7UxU\nS0Kr1shoZb3nGUwY4bTS\n=FEYd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d8830adee5baa50596b8bf00961c5a06cde582fd\nparent 6332c25a675b14eb4bd9ba17041b534e4c1c1750\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1779949261 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779949261 +0300\n\nfix(version-compat): bump MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION to 2.6.4 (#242)\n\nCompanion PR to #234 (urgent v2.6.3 group-chat compaction-wedge hotfix).\n\nWithout this bump, v2.6.3 nodes wouldn't auto-deploy to v2.6.4 — the\nheartbeat handler gates auto-deploy on `plugin_version <\nMIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION`. With the previous floor of 2.6.3,\nexisting 2.6.3 nodes sit at the threshold and the deploy command never\nfires.\n\nSame release-process gap PRs #204 (2.5.0 → 2.6.2) and #226 (2.6.2 →\n2.6.3) closed.\n\n## Merge order\nShould be merged **after** PR #234 lands (so the new plugin code is on\nmain when this bump tells the server to push it).\n\n## Follow-up\nHave release-please auto-sync this constant from plugin/package.json so\nwe don't need a manual companion PR per plugin release. Tracked\nseparately.\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-05-28T06:21:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f5668f6d0e99ee4f3d4612c8dbdafcaff2a8bb13","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f5668f6d0e99ee4f3d4612c8dbdafcaff2a8bb13","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f5668f6d0e99ee4f3d4612c8dbdafcaff2a8bb13/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6332c25a675b14eb4bd9ba17041b534e4c1c1750","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6332c25a675b14eb4bd9ba17041b534e4c1c1750","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/6332c25a675b14eb4bd9ba17041b534e4c1c1750"}]},{"sha":"6332c25a675b14eb4bd9ba17041b534e4c1c1750","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDYzMzJjMjVhNjc1YjE0ZWI0YmQ5YmExNzA0MWI1MzRlNGMxYzE3NTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-27T18:51:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-27T18:51:37Z"},"message":"feat(events): subscription manifest to guard infra provisioning (#240)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds a machine-readable contract of **which Pub/Sub topics each deployed\nservice subscribes to**, so the infra repo (caura-memclaw-enterprise)\ncan fail CI when a consumed topic lacks a provisioned subscription.\n\nThis is the OSS half of a guard against the failure that took staging\ndown: OSS #238 added `memclaw.lifecycle.insights-requested` with a\ncore-api subscriber, but no Terraform subscription existed — core-api's\npull loop 404'd, `/api/v1/health` 503'd, and `deploy-to-staging` failed\non every run.\n\n- `common/events/events_manifest.json` — `{service: [topics]}` for\nPubSub/SaaS deployment mode.\n- `scripts/gen_events_manifest.py` — generator (`--check` mode for CI).\nLifecycle topics are captured **dynamically** by invoking\n`register_pipeline_consumers` / `register_archive_consumers` against a\nrecording bus, so a new `bus.subscribe` in a helper is picked up\nautomatically. Memory-pipeline direct subscribes are listed explicitly\n(OSS CI doesn't install the worker package, so it can't be imported\nhere).\n- `tests/test_events/test_events_manifest.py` — fails if the committed\nmanifest drifts from the generator (runs in the existing `pytest tests/`\nCI step; no workflow change).\n\n## How the guard works end-to-end\n1. Dev adds a consumed topic (e.g. to a lifecycle helper) → this test\nfails until they run `python scripts/gen_events_manifest.py` → manifest\nupdated.\n2. The enterprise repo's `check_pubsub_provisioning.py` reads this\nmanifest and fails its CI until a matching\n`${var.env}-<service>--<topic>` Terraform subscription exists.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `python scripts/gen_events_manifest.py --check` passes\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_events/test_events_manifest.py` passes (2\ntests)\n- [x] ruff check + format clean\n- [ ] Manifest reviewed: core-api = {embedded, enriched, crystallize,\nentity-link, insights}; core-worker = {embed-requested,\nenrich-requested, archive-expired, archive-stale, purge-soft-deleted}\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"4a5b4d16d2719db2ab730d80d84b07c93b331e89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/4a5b4d16d2719db2ab730d80d84b07c93b331e89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/6332c25a675b14eb4bd9ba17041b534e4c1c1750","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqFz05CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUGcQAJ+5eieOayNnvmK2WE83+0Do\nyqD7ephVg7bWaWPbzGSa0PviVmszSfMLgSxvcf+ctdKqL13m2EGqGsfxWKUBDL9g\nGF01TxxwvPQYhBbKU/7zUsBlkpFoJEMLQSR9OKGcVS6jtnsfJZvwFki898L/kvo2\nhCUX+pLYNHlo1dSCdKxfH7HsotgpJzH11Sgpeve4nQlzruWzT4yQi+5sEWgLvPlt\nuA0qOdTO8VnUJVlyL3QKyplXGk0tv1QUl6VLuB4SGRZIDkqv4IgSJEmH64rI4Dys\n30VZE+qenfkWcg74h++ufJGNmug1k8/ty3CbEgBwXlmQewqaE9gJVmCNcluGmpIo\nbLp5wppi93Acj8dcTFq4z3hPMkFIIMy0TEhLmonPv+2BcJqoVt9qWIDzCtzPUFGu\ntRMOcwEQAiEJIQd62CHf+GNgizjl5diCYAUoyJDW/HcmZ63Ub4YdphkwKzhtW0Ld\nWHZNZu2mcA5dO6BnlnDSm9nbKdztAFuoZTDUr2ICYR2or3H8Tda1AIRpc6R0as8O\n0WnQlikWh8p5WMIuPhO4u0BhPkD5htiSgTN4gM+mxcA6F1R96+b2cOj/KiQfa1yK\no3lBzWh5e0YfxGpBnSPXd9UmI1XMjP3OANPymNukCo5y4OIWrVjvtKaXG0AgHG9J\n96Wb2d12IsStII7bYItZ\n=ovhS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4a5b4d16d2719db2ab730d80d84b07c93b331e89\nparent 751108c7bf320841105d85a06cf117341e86b913\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1779907897 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779907897 +0300\n\nfeat(events): subscription manifest to guard infra provisioning (#240)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds a machine-readable contract of **which Pub/Sub topics each deployed\nservice subscribes to**, so the infra repo (caura-memclaw-enterprise)\ncan fail CI when a consumed topic lacks a provisioned subscription.\n\nThis is the OSS half of a guard against the failure that took staging\ndown: OSS #238 added `memclaw.lifecycle.insights-requested` with a\ncore-api subscriber, but no Terraform subscription existed — core-api's\npull loop 404'd, `/api/v1/health` 503'd, and `deploy-to-staging` failed\non every run.\n\n- `common/events/events_manifest.json` — `{service: [topics]}` for\nPubSub/SaaS deployment mode.\n- `scripts/gen_events_manifest.py` — generator (`--check` mode for CI).\nLifecycle topics are captured **dynamically** by invoking\n`register_pipeline_consumers` / `register_archive_consumers` against a\nrecording bus, so a new `bus.subscribe` in a helper is picked up\nautomatically. Memory-pipeline direct subscribes are listed explicitly\n(OSS CI doesn't install the worker package, so it can't be imported\nhere).\n- `tests/test_events/test_events_manifest.py` — fails if the committed\nmanifest drifts from the generator (runs in the existing `pytest tests/`\nCI step; no workflow change).\n\n## How the guard works end-to-end\n1. Dev adds a consumed topic (e.g. to a lifecycle helper) → this test\nfails until they run `python scripts/gen_events_manifest.py` → manifest\nupdated.\n2. The enterprise repo's `check_pubsub_provisioning.py` reads this\nmanifest and fails its CI until a matching\n`${var.env}-<service>--<topic>` Terraform subscription exists.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `python scripts/gen_events_manifest.py --check` passes\n- [x] `pytest tests/test_events/test_events_manifest.py` passes (2\ntests)\n- [x] ruff check + format clean\n- [ ] Manifest reviewed: core-api = {embedded, enriched, crystallize,\nentity-link, insights}; core-worker = {embed-requested,\nenrich-requested, archive-expired, archive-stale, purge-soft-deleted}\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-05-27T18:51:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6332c25a675b14eb4bd9ba17041b534e4c1c1750","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/6332c25a675b14eb4bd9ba17041b534e4c1c1750","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/6332c25a675b14eb4bd9ba17041b534e4c1c1750/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"751108c7bf320841105d85a06cf117341e86b913","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/751108c7bf320841105d85a06cf117341e86b913","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/751108c7bf320841105d85a06cf117341e86b913"}]},{"sha":"751108c7bf320841105d85a06cf117341e86b913","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDc1MTEwOGM3YmYzMjA4NDExMDVkODVhMDZjZjExNzM0MWU4NmI5MTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-27T15:36:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-27T15:36:04Z"},"message":"perf(crystallizer): collapse archive-sweep N+1 storage HTTPs (P5) (#239)\n\n## Summary\n\nAudit P5 — ``_run_crystallization`` issued one storage HTTP per\ncandidate id (``get_memory``) plus one per cluster member\n(``update_memory_status``) during the archive sweep. Replaced with the\nbulk endpoints from PR #222.\n\n## Sites collapsed\n\n| Loop | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Loop 1 (lines 312-316) | Per-id ``sc.get_memory`` across all\n``total_ids`` | One ``sc.bulk_get_memories`` |\n| Loop 2 (lines 354-361, inside per-cluster body) | Per-row\n``sc.update_memory_status(mid, \"archived\")`` | One\n``sc.batch_update_status`` per cluster (K HTTPs instead of K × M) |\n\nPer-cluster failure isolation preserved — one cluster's archive failure\ndoesn't kill the rest of the sweep, matching the prior per-row\ntry/except shape at cluster granularity.\n\n## Behavior preserved\n\n- Skipped rows (CAS miss, deleted, nonexistent) drop from the\n``memories_archived`` count via the batch response's ``skipped`` list —\nsame wire effect the old per-row try/except branch gave us. Any\nnon-empty ``skipped`` is logged at WARN.\n- ``bulk_get_memories``'s aligned ``None`` slots preserve the prior ``if\nmem:`` skip semantic for deleted ids.\n- Empty candidate set → no bulk HTTP fires (avoid empty round-trip).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] New ``tests/test_p5_crystallizer_archive_sweep.py`` (5 tests)\nasserts shape directly: one bulk_get + one batch per cluster, zero\nper-row HTTPs, skipped-rows accounting, empty-pairs short-circuit,\nNone-slot handling for deleted ids.\n- [x] Existing ``test_p5_crystallizer.py`` +\n``test_api_crystallizer.py`` stay green (33 tests).\n- [x] Full unit sweep: **1327 passing**.\n- [x] Ruff lint + format clean.\n- [x] mypy clean (pre-existing ``config.py`` croniter stub error\nunrelated).\n\n## Audit queue status after this PR\n\n| Audit ID | PR | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| B4 | #217 | merged |\n| P1/P2/P5 storage foundation | #222 | merged |\n| T5 + #22/#25/#29/#31 | #235 | merged |\n| P2 (contradiction batch) | #236 | merged |\n| **P5 (this PR)** | — | open |\n| P1 (entity-extraction bulk) | — | next |\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: ran-taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"31f740e9483db21bf96f9d7b65e6c9224291da77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/31f740e9483db21bf96f9d7b65e6c9224291da77"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/751108c7bf320841105d85a06cf117341e86b913","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqFw9kCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlm8QAFvS5u5xY92oXCfoZ0JHmw5U\nMgQPrihzXkXkaAw8zHyDyDUecDvtOMBKoYGmlcYS6Q1H4tWQqio+afdiD7jbZ8eY\n6ZH4/hnbgStydU1fzBIeuLYQek4nFOy6/Kd72ps32AEbuJ6aQZChKVQsybSfjSDt\nSuZcd/5YzIKqOoaHi1Mjzu31nLnIJEuHCVbwX+o+wnEhb6keCBLbrhTNXdgU9wMy\nHOhI98hD2Qj92ce27gQbjgmZDoPU8NRvMAL0McNTMhTaWfQfhCh7/UAdgHrfTLmX\nhYxj81sK8Ng2zCWZLhQCEOQVuto28w49zuG9R3YGDJ1NThifKPctY9e9pl6LSkB2\nXYeCi+J1NAc6xBGx15kVtjGV4kURSLnaMnEykig4My8R+I/72q8RZeXImLMzk6pB\nVK7lraYeJENPMxZtbU7hBRrYNSaGNmWuajToMXzunabxR976GoHBzuBdwVoBg1qp\n1OJj0kV/3O7XiwYSOjOipMlar4jUY7b+RroahUmrgxcyCFksiSgvyHfQNUqaHisq\nUQhUtq0L0m2WvrDqn7OYS9P2qk3tmFnvz+h5rlafbG/NTFll0+bSQ/ksSxKWbpbn\n/YqWYMi4ao8TVZAslJWApq6sIEk9cQFt1h+23Uf0Mk8KcOK5ENpw74sVFDQoIXe8\nMCE9hDZQ9/uekFI/IQu2\n=31Ed\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 31f740e9483db21bf96f9d7b65e6c9224291da77\nparent bfa5dbb254b7c770a77929c7cb396106b6964223\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1779896164 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779896164 +0300\n\nperf(crystallizer): collapse archive-sweep N+1 storage HTTPs (P5) (#239)\n\n## Summary\n\nAudit P5 — ``_run_crystallization`` issued one storage HTTP per\ncandidate id (``get_memory``) plus one per cluster member\n(``update_memory_status``) during the archive sweep. Replaced with the\nbulk endpoints from PR #222.\n\n## Sites collapsed\n\n| Loop | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Loop 1 (lines 312-316) | Per-id ``sc.get_memory`` across all\n``total_ids`` | One ``sc.bulk_get_memories`` |\n| Loop 2 (lines 354-361, inside per-cluster body) | Per-row\n``sc.update_memory_status(mid, \"archived\")`` | One\n``sc.batch_update_status`` per cluster (K HTTPs instead of K × M) |\n\nPer-cluster failure isolation preserved — one cluster's archive failure\ndoesn't kill the rest of the sweep, matching the prior per-row\ntry/except shape at cluster granularity.\n\n## Behavior preserved\n\n- Skipped rows (CAS miss, deleted, nonexistent) drop from the\n``memories_archived`` count via the batch response's ``skipped`` list —\nsame wire effect the old per-row try/except branch gave us. Any\nnon-empty ``skipped`` is logged at WARN.\n- ``bulk_get_memories``'s aligned ``None`` slots preserve the prior ``if\nmem:`` skip semantic for deleted ids.\n- Empty candidate set → no bulk HTTP fires (avoid empty round-trip).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] New ``tests/test_p5_crystallizer_archive_sweep.py`` (5 tests)\nasserts shape directly: one bulk_get + one batch per cluster, zero\nper-row HTTPs, skipped-rows accounting, empty-pairs short-circuit,\nNone-slot handling for deleted ids.\n- [x] Existing ``test_p5_crystallizer.py`` +\n``test_api_crystallizer.py`` stay green (33 tests).\n- [x] Full unit sweep: **1327 passing**.\n- [x] Ruff lint + format clean.\n- [x] mypy clean (pre-existing ``config.py`` croniter stub error\nunrelated).\n\n## Audit queue status after this PR\n\n| Audit ID | PR | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| B4 | #217 | merged |\n| P1/P2/P5 storage foundation | #222 | merged |\n| T5 + #22/#25/#29/#31 | #235 | merged |\n| P2 (contradiction batch) | #236 | merged |\n| **P5 (this PR)** | — | open |\n| P1 (entity-extraction bulk) | — | next |\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: ran-taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-27T15:36:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/751108c7bf320841105d85a06cf117341e86b913","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/751108c7bf320841105d85a06cf117341e86b913","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/751108c7bf320841105d85a06cf117341e86b913/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bfa5dbb254b7c770a77929c7cb396106b6964223","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bfa5dbb254b7c770a77929c7cb396106b6964223","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/bfa5dbb254b7c770a77929c7cb396106b6964223"}]},{"sha":"bfa5dbb254b7c770a77929c7cb396106b6964223","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGJmYTVkYmIyNTRiN2M3NzBhNzc5MjljN2NiMzk2MTA2YjY5NjQyMjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-27T14:21:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-27T14:21:01Z"},"message":"chore(perf+sec+tests): ran follow-ups — T5 + #22/#25/#29/#31 (#235)\n\n## Summary\n\nFive small, independent fixes from the audit follow-up queue. Each is\ncontained to one file and none depends on the others — could be split\ninto 5 PRs, bundled here for review efficiency since the per-change LOC\nis small.\n\n| Audit ID | Surface | Type | LOC |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **T5** | tests/conftest.py — `_patch_storage_client` fixture | Test\nhygiene (cross-test leak) | +5 |\n| **#22** | routes/crystallizer.py — `get_report` | Security\n(cross-tenant existence leak) | +6 |\n| **#25** | services/evolve_service.py — `_apply_outcome_to_db` | Perf\n(N+1 UPDATE → single statement) | ~80 |\n| **#29** | services/insights_service.py — `_persist_findings` | Perf\n(serial create_memory → create_memories_bulk) | ~75 |\n| **#31** | services/entity_extraction_worker.py | Cleanup (dead\ntry/except) | de-indent only |\n\n## Per-fix detail\n\n### T5 — try/finally on `_patch_storage_client`\nThe autouse fixture mutated `sc_mod._client` then `yield`ed. A\nsetup-time exception between the mutation and yield (or any teardown\nerror) would leak the ASGI-bridged client into subsequent tests via the\nmodule-level singleton — caused intermittent cascade failures\npreviously. Wrap in try/finally.\n\n### #22 — 404 (not 403) for foreign-tenant report read\n`GET /crystallize/reports/{id}` used to 404 on missing rows but **403**\non foreign-tenant rows (via `enforce_tenant`). Two distinguishable\nstates let attackers enumerate cross-tenant report_ids by random-probing\nUUIDs (403 = exists in another tenant; 404 = doesn't exist anywhere).\nCollapse both to 404 with the same detail. Admin keys keep cross-tenant\nread via the `is_admin` bypass.\n\n### #25 — Collapse evolve_service N+1 weight UPDATEs\nOne UPDATE per `related_id` inside its own savepoint → single `UPDATE\nFROM (VALUES …)` via `IN :mids` expanding bindparam. One outer savepoint\npreserves the \"DB failure aborts the bulk but not the outer transaction\"\ncontract. Per-row response ordering and the \"row-not-found → skip with\nwarning\" semantics preserved.\n\n### #29 — Use `create_memories_bulk` in insights findings persist\nSerial `create_memory` per finding inside per-finding savepoint → single\n`create_memories_bulk` call. Per-item error isolation comes from the\nbulk contract (`BulkItemResult(status=\"error\")` → `None` in\n`insight_ids`). Empty-findings short-circuit added\n(`BulkMemoryCreate.items` enforces `min_length=1`).\n\n### #31 — Delete dead try/except\nInner `try: ... except Exception: raise` re-raised into the outer except\none frame above — pure no-op. Removed the wrapper and de-indented the\nbody. Smaller stack on logged exceptions; cleaner blame.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] **2 new regression tests** in `tests/test_api_crystallizer.py` for\n#22:\n- `test_get_report_foreign_tenant_returns_404_not_403`: non-admin\ncaller, foreign report → 404 (asserts via direct route call with mocked\nAuthContext + storage client; no HTTP fixture required).\n- `test_get_report_foreign_tenant_admin_bypass`: admin still reads\ncross-tenant.\n- [x] **Updated**\n`tests/test_insights_service.py::test_priors_restored_when_all_findings_fail`\nto patch `create_memories_bulk` (the new persist target) instead of\n`create_memory`. Still exercises the \"all findings failed → restore\npriors\" branch.\n- [x] **218 tests pass** across touched surfaces (storage bulk\nendpoints, entity linking, insights, crystallizer, evolve, A4 status,\nA10 evolve rule, MCP insights, entity blocklist, A5c tenant config).\n- [x] Ruff lint + format clean.\n- [x] mypy on core-api clean (only pre-existing `config.py` croniter\nstub from main).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: ran-taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3c211bc31cf92019b949d022dc98ac8a4dd39874","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/3c211bc31cf92019b949d022dc98ac8a4dd39874"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/bfa5dbb254b7c770a77929c7cb396106b6964223","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqFv3NCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHUkQAG1KuFZmRVRltabQRDQjxqeJ\nlzv7nMTwKXG+Sme+H5JRNbjut5Ahhird3ZaqMZ5ortFVGweTOOH6JIHtH3LJ4LL6\nHILY6y2oN9rV9to2qnopK0ykpFHYz5/t5sM1CbPgPbpNTq8OM9VnoI0PQ+uULjSL\nvi89W8dZBsOMAkLm4rKXRp+HuGVDhTpaVkcPyvkitvMfVLJEuNCAWdNQAJXdSM21\nVYQ02niiCxTnIi2JJXDT8FHBSdVHF+2Cc33Uzog9d4vPcWUh1Y9X0hpnaQRxVN5H\ny2kJRpav/ASk9WmZc4QWcbaeqGJzDY9T/PToNazP6ltblNm/TVEpsRd7b1V+cA7b\ns/CSXdqDkmXyjEyqt0yOtj43n7TFXVbasaovV7z87NcwWXAoMCYmzzFMWtUtxUZB\neKubd9o5gvE8X9YwflekUrt8Pz5fjF6ZlsZs4MUkDEVpXxWqCM7U58/VvmHCbuTb\niJByDZY4wdZPspDGBopsFgmiRTq8VRpJa4HOWyz5JDeXiSyzkKCy96R59IKeOLs1\nnbGdtgSZB2XI7sFgvN/tCySUgh0GvpJsE7lwa+hiNlTM3rZfRPv5+3WmdI1PQ1gJ\nD9O7YMEucVAc93rbyGSKiGE9vONilM+3ds7SHUjWGnKRTQcy3E5VCA3RlJvaT98q\nsuv+MdYOr9QGgCWWARqP\n=D0tQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3c211bc31cf92019b949d022dc98ac8a4dd39874\nparent f5de6f67049301dd6ece1061c444d0ef0ad2bea0\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1779891661 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779891661 +0300\n\nchore(perf+sec+tests): ran follow-ups — T5 + #22/#25/#29/#31 (#235)\n\n## Summary\n\nFive small, independent fixes from the audit follow-up queue. Each is\ncontained to one file and none depends on the others — could be split\ninto 5 PRs, bundled here for review efficiency since the per-change LOC\nis small.\n\n| Audit ID | Surface | Type | LOC |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **T5** | tests/conftest.py — `_patch_storage_client` fixture | Test\nhygiene (cross-test leak) | +5 |\n| **#22** | routes/crystallizer.py — `get_report` | Security\n(cross-tenant existence leak) | +6 |\n| **#25** | services/evolve_service.py — `_apply_outcome_to_db` | Perf\n(N+1 UPDATE → single statement) | ~80 |\n| **#29** | services/insights_service.py — `_persist_findings` | Perf\n(serial create_memory → create_memories_bulk) | ~75 |\n| **#31** | services/entity_extraction_worker.py | Cleanup (dead\ntry/except) | de-indent only |\n\n## Per-fix detail\n\n### T5 — try/finally on `_patch_storage_client`\nThe autouse fixture mutated `sc_mod._client` then `yield`ed. A\nsetup-time exception between the mutation and yield (or any teardown\nerror) would leak the ASGI-bridged client into subsequent tests via the\nmodule-level singleton — caused intermittent cascade failures\npreviously. Wrap in try/finally.\n\n### #22 — 404 (not 403) for foreign-tenant report read\n`GET /crystallize/reports/{id}` used to 404 on missing rows but **403**\non foreign-tenant rows (via `enforce_tenant`). Two distinguishable\nstates let attackers enumerate cross-tenant report_ids by random-probing\nUUIDs (403 = exists in another tenant; 404 = doesn't exist anywhere).\nCollapse both to 404 with the same detail. Admin keys keep cross-tenant\nread via the `is_admin` bypass.\n\n### #25 — Collapse evolve_service N+1 weight UPDATEs\nOne UPDATE per `related_id` inside its own savepoint → single `UPDATE\nFROM (VALUES …)` via `IN :mids` expanding bindparam. One outer savepoint\npreserves the \"DB failure aborts the bulk but not the outer transaction\"\ncontract. Per-row response ordering and the \"row-not-found → skip with\nwarning\" semantics preserved.\n\n### #29 — Use `create_memories_bulk` in insights findings persist\nSerial `create_memory` per finding inside per-finding savepoint → single\n`create_memories_bulk` call. Per-item error isolation comes from the\nbulk contract (`BulkItemResult(status=\"error\")` → `None` in\n`insight_ids`). Empty-findings short-circuit added\n(`BulkMemoryCreate.items` enforces `min_length=1`).\n\n### #31 — Delete dead try/except\nInner `try: ... except Exception: raise` re-raised into the outer except\none frame above — pure no-op. Removed the wrapper and de-indented the\nbody. Smaller stack on logged exceptions; cleaner blame.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] **2 new regression tests** in `tests/test_api_crystallizer.py` for\n#22:\n- `test_get_report_foreign_tenant_returns_404_not_403`: non-admin\ncaller, foreign report → 404 (asserts via direct route call with mocked\nAuthContext + storage client; no HTTP fixture required).\n- `test_get_report_foreign_tenant_admin_bypass`: admin still reads\ncross-tenant.\n- [x] **Updated**\n`tests/test_insights_service.py::test_priors_restored_when_all_findings_fail`\nto patch `create_memories_bulk` (the new persist target) instead of\n`create_memory`. Still exercises the \"all findings failed → restore\npriors\" branch.\n- [x] **218 tests pass** across touched surfaces (storage bulk\nendpoints, entity linking, insights, crystallizer, evolve, A4 status,\nA10 evolve rule, MCP insights, entity blocklist, A5c tenant config).\n- [x] Ruff lint + format clean.\n- [x] mypy on core-api clean (only pre-existing `config.py` croniter\nstub from main).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: ran-taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-27T14:21:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bfa5dbb254b7c770a77929c7cb396106b6964223","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/bfa5dbb254b7c770a77929c7cb396106b6964223","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/bfa5dbb254b7c770a77929c7cb396106b6964223/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f5de6f67049301dd6ece1061c444d0ef0ad2bea0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f5de6f67049301dd6ece1061c444d0ef0ad2bea0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f5de6f67049301dd6ece1061c444d0ef0ad2bea0"}]},{"sha":"f5de6f67049301dd6ece1061c444d0ef0ad2bea0","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGY1ZGU2ZjY3MDQ5MzAxZGQ2ZWNlMTA2MWM0NDRkMGVmMGFkMmJlYTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"eyal-bl","email":"eyal.b@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-27T14:07:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-27T14:07:06Z"},"message":"CAURA-687 fix(search): wire ENTITY_LOOKUP short-circuit to dedicated … (#237)\n\n…storage endpoint\n\nThe ENTITY_LOOKUP short-circuit in ClassifyQuery._collect_memories\nposted a payload with ``memory_ids`` + ``entity_lookup: True`` to\n``/memories/ scored-search``, but that route never read those keys — it\nhard-indexed ``body[\"embedding\"]`` and 500'd. The broad ``except\nException:`` at classify_query.py:123 swallowed the failure and the\npipeline silently fell through to keyword/semantic search on every\nentity-token query.\n\nThis was the second bug in the same code path. CAURA-684 fixed the dict-\nvs-tuple shape mismatch at _expand_per_fleet line 214; once that landed\nthe next gate (_collect_memories → scored_search) became reachable and\nits contract bug surfaced as a storage 500 (confirmed live in staging\n2026-05-27: same query, same fallthrough warning, but trace now ends at\nKeyError 'embedding' on the storage side instead of KeyError 0 on the\nclient side).\n\nAdopts Approach A from the design discussion:\n\n- New storage method ``PostgresService.memory_load_by_ids`` that selects\nmemories by ID with visibility/fleet/agent/memory_type/status/valid_at\nfilters lifted verbatim from ``memory_scored_search``. No vector cosine,\nno FTS, no freshness scoring — sub-millisecond ``SELECT WHERE id IN\n(...)``. Filter clauses MUST stay in sync with ``memory_scored_search``\n(any drift is a cross-tenant leak risk — comment notes this for future\nmaintainers).\n\n- New route ``POST /memories/load-by-ids`` (dedicated endpoint rather\nthan a conditional branch inside ``/memories/scored-search`` — clearer\ncontract, smaller blast radius, easier to test).\n\n- New storage client method ``load_memories_by_ids``.\n\n- ``_collect_memories`` switches the call from ``scored_search`` to\n``load_memories_by_ids``. Also now forwards ``valid_at`` and\n``readable_tenant_ids`` which were silently dropped before — the\nshort-circuit's visibility behaviour now matches the scored-search\nfallthrough exactly. Drops the unused ``entity_lookup: True`` flag.\n\nTests:\n\n- tests/test_entity_lookup_short_circuit.py: switched the storage mock\nto ``load_memories_by_ids``. Added two assertions: (1) ``valid_at`` +\n``readable_tenant_ids`` are forwarded in the cross-tenant case. (2)\n``readable_tenant_ids`` is OMITTED in the single-tenant case so storage\nuses the cheap ``tenant_id == X`` predicate. Both also assert the old\nstale keys (``embedding``/``query``/\n``search_params``/``entity_lookup``) are absent from the payload.\n\n- tests/pipeline/test_classify_query.py: switched the four ENTITY_LOOKUP\ntest paths' mocks from ``scored_search`` to ``load_memories_by_ids``,\nplus the ``_mock_sc`` default. The remaining scored_search default stays\nfor non-ENTITY_LOOKUP test paths.\n\nFollow-up worth a separate ticket: tighten the broad ``except\nException:`` at classify_query.py:123 to catch only expected exception\ntypes so the next regression doesn't take months to surface.\n\n<!-- Thanks for the contribution! Please fill in this template so we can\nreview quickly. -->\n\n## Summary\n\n<!-- What does this PR do? One or two sentences. -->\n\n## Related Issue\n\n<!-- Link the issue this PR addresses, e.g. `Closes #123`. Delete if\nN/A. -->\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change that fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change that adds functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that changes existing behavior)\n- [ ] Documentation update\n- [ ] Refactor / internal cleanup\n- [ ] Other:\n\n## How Has This Been Tested?\n\n<!-- Describe the tests you ran. Include commands if possible. -->\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [ ] I have added tests that cover my changes (or explained why none\nare needed)\n- [ ] `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` pass\n- [ ] `mypy` passes\n- [ ] `pytest` passes locally\n- [ ] I have updated relevant documentation (README,\nARCHITECTURE_REVIEW, etc.)\n- [ ] I have updated `CHANGELOG.md` under the `Unreleased` section (if\nuser-facing)\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n<!-- Anything reviewers should know — tradeoffs, follow-up work, open\nquestions. -->\n\nSigned-off-by: Eyal Blyachman <eyal.b@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"6db759a9f13b4883360fe6239438d5aff337651a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/6db759a9f13b4883360fe6239438d5aff337651a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/f5de6f67049301dd6ece1061c444d0ef0ad2bea0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqFvqKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABcEQACr5KJZpaTdcKvdyqNgCykCE\n9d+5RttVJAtmWE8S6TuRbfaV1yiUqLymFptNWOlNxS//Xw+XJajKcu2Ukxy9ovtH\nPkxW/282ae1w6FphBkaPjCmS+2nxz7nwQCgAqwoQ4RDNzNV6OMPaja9BGwqkDfiJ\nGueoGJ/kcnOAGQ9Inrt35dIs1oCCUAHu4i3IFJAFCd5KwRvsx0h4KGnzrmlZRqDb\n86nmXUXhv/nExP94W12AGnqwUhiOK8cksnLoom8UuKecMN3lV8oqk8N3y4BzadT2\npB+/1NAD2kerF+jrnHCcSE2EoJQRVI54GHpuzn6MLOHyLHMioD75y/Yc6oHOCaUa\nFvt/4/wAs1l0uY7b+BSOzoR6pHAlTNqrndaKYUAHH5oZa+mf64O0SCcDikzr4Hlg\n2QYAA5C7ilwfE6LytzUh73LhKZj+oN5Bo4S7I402vSEC24L1SgRk4NRThwo5mBt/\nxQSI/p+k0oOE/ELdKUHNAuwdcj0ZWJfCrIJyH2Z6ZE2Z6sh2FJIJ0jxYzGFAkotf\nEbzPHlrhyTxig7Fe6ddz/X9YDEk3WGuIMRX0o4G9bQxe6AQ9FG5D/j7EMct8/M/J\nbvUr9U+FF3pnBTqRIQqUqAtLPXFEGu54nd/9g350xMHArfKOjYvoXJBePtcIvr6x\ny12IEM2O5f+VLv7qssw4\n=5cI+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6db759a9f13b4883360fe6239438d5aff337651a\nparent 2c8942c0b88039aa6cc7b8990420ea39a3de26c1\nauthor eyal-bl <eyal.b@caura.ai> 1779890826 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779890826 +0300\n\nCAURA-687 fix(search): wire ENTITY_LOOKUP short-circuit to dedicated … (#237)\n\n…storage endpoint\n\nThe ENTITY_LOOKUP short-circuit in ClassifyQuery._collect_memories\nposted a payload with ``memory_ids`` + ``entity_lookup: True`` to\n``/memories/ scored-search``, but that route never read those keys — it\nhard-indexed ``body[\"embedding\"]`` and 500'd. The broad ``except\nException:`` at classify_query.py:123 swallowed the failure and the\npipeline silently fell through to keyword/semantic search on every\nentity-token query.\n\nThis was the second bug in the same code path. CAURA-684 fixed the dict-\nvs-tuple shape mismatch at _expand_per_fleet line 214; once that landed\nthe next gate (_collect_memories → scored_search) became reachable and\nits contract bug surfaced as a storage 500 (confirmed live in staging\n2026-05-27: same query, same fallthrough warning, but trace now ends at\nKeyError 'embedding' on the storage side instead of KeyError 0 on the\nclient side).\n\nAdopts Approach A from the design discussion:\n\n- New storage method ``PostgresService.memory_load_by_ids`` that selects\nmemories by ID with visibility/fleet/agent/memory_type/status/valid_at\nfilters lifted verbatim from ``memory_scored_search``. No vector cosine,\nno FTS, no freshness scoring — sub-millisecond ``SELECT WHERE id IN\n(...)``. Filter clauses MUST stay in sync with ``memory_scored_search``\n(any drift is a cross-tenant leak risk — comment notes this for future\nmaintainers).\n\n- New route ``POST /memories/load-by-ids`` (dedicated endpoint rather\nthan a conditional branch inside ``/memories/scored-search`` — clearer\ncontract, smaller blast radius, easier to test).\n\n- New storage client method ``load_memories_by_ids``.\n\n- ``_collect_memories`` switches the call from ``scored_search`` to\n``load_memories_by_ids``. Also now forwards ``valid_at`` and\n``readable_tenant_ids`` which were silently dropped before — the\nshort-circuit's visibility behaviour now matches the scored-search\nfallthrough exactly. Drops the unused ``entity_lookup: True`` flag.\n\nTests:\n\n- tests/test_entity_lookup_short_circuit.py: switched the storage mock\nto ``load_memories_by_ids``. Added two assertions: (1) ``valid_at`` +\n``readable_tenant_ids`` are forwarded in the cross-tenant case. (2)\n``readable_tenant_ids`` is OMITTED in the single-tenant case so storage\nuses the cheap ``tenant_id == X`` predicate. Both also assert the old\nstale keys (``embedding``/``query``/\n``search_params``/``entity_lookup``) are absent from the payload.\n\n- tests/pipeline/test_classify_query.py: switched the four ENTITY_LOOKUP\ntest paths' mocks from ``scored_search`` to ``load_memories_by_ids``,\nplus the ``_mock_sc`` default. The remaining scored_search default stays\nfor non-ENTITY_LOOKUP test paths.\n\nFollow-up worth a separate ticket: tighten the broad ``except\nException:`` at classify_query.py:123 to catch only expected exception\ntypes so the next regression doesn't take months to surface.\n\n<!-- Thanks for the contribution! Please fill in this template so we can\nreview quickly. -->\n\n## Summary\n\n<!-- What does this PR do? One or two sentences. -->\n\n## Related Issue\n\n<!-- Link the issue this PR addresses, e.g. `Closes #123`. Delete if\nN/A. -->\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change that fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change that adds functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that changes existing behavior)\n- [ ] Documentation update\n- [ ] Refactor / internal cleanup\n- [ ] Other:\n\n## How Has This Been Tested?\n\n<!-- Describe the tests you ran. Include commands if possible. -->\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [ ] I have added tests that cover my changes (or explained why none\nare needed)\n- [ ] `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` pass\n- [ ] `mypy` passes\n- [ ] `pytest` passes locally\n- [ ] I have updated relevant documentation (README,\nARCHITECTURE_REVIEW, etc.)\n- [ ] I have updated `CHANGELOG.md` under the `Unreleased` section (if\nuser-facing)\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n<!-- Anything reviewers should know — tradeoffs, follow-up work, open\nquestions. -->\n\nSigned-off-by: Eyal Blyachman <eyal.b@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-05-27T14:07:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f5de6f67049301dd6ece1061c444d0ef0ad2bea0","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f5de6f67049301dd6ece1061c444d0ef0ad2bea0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f5de6f67049301dd6ece1061c444d0ef0ad2bea0/comments","author":{"login":"eyal-bl","id":262085605,"node_id":"U_kgDOD58b5Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262085605?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl","html_url":"https://github.com/eyal-bl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyal-bl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2c8942c0b88039aa6cc7b8990420ea39a3de26c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2c8942c0b88039aa6cc7b8990420ea39a3de26c1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2c8942c0b88039aa6cc7b8990420ea39a3de26c1"}]},{"sha":"2c8942c0b88039aa6cc7b8990420ea39a3de26c1","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDJjODk0MmMwYjg4MDM5YWE2Y2M3Yjg5OTA0MjBlYTM5YTNkZTI2YzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-05-27T13:14:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-27T13:14:50Z"},"message":"perf(contradiction): collapse N+1 status updates into batch_update_status per path (P2) (#236)\n\n## Summary\n\nAudit P2 — the contradiction detector issued up to **3K**\n`update_memory_status` HTTPs per detection cycle (K conflicts × 3 call\nshapes per match), all serial, after the parallel LLM `asyncio.gather`.\nThe `batch_update_status` storage endpoint (widened in #222) was sitting\nwith zero callers. This PR is its first consumer.\n\n## Sites collapsed (9 → 3 batch flushes)\n\n| Path | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Semantic (`_detect`, post-gather loop) | 3 call shapes at lines\n433/446/463 | 1 `batch_update_status` |\n| Path C (`detect_contradictions_by_entities_async`) | 3 call shapes at\nlines 1064/1075/1092 | 1 `batch_update_status` |\n| RDF (`_detect`, `for old in rdf_conflicts`) | 3 call shapes at lines\n300/322/347 | 1 `batch_update_status` |\n\n`_attempt_path_c_retraction`'s two sequential `update_memory_status`\ncalls stay — they're not in a loop, only 2 calls; collapsing costs more\nclarity than it saves.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] New `tests/test_p2_contradiction_batch_status.py` (5 tests) —\nasserts shape directly: exactly one `batch_update_status` per cycle,\nzero per-row `update_memory_status`, correct payload contents per path,\nempty paths skip the HTTP, gather-exception isolation\n- [x] Legacy `mock_sc.update_memory_status.call_args_list` assertions in\n7 test files stay green via\n`tests/_contradiction_batch_compat.install_batch_status_replay_shim` — a\none-line addition per test setup that routes the batch call back to\nper-row mock invocations, sparing ~80 mechanical assertion migrations\n- [x] Full contradiction-related sweep: **144/144** unit tests pass\n(`test_contradiction_*`, `test_a4_*`, `test_p1_contradiction`,\n`test_p2_contradiction_batch_status`, `test_visibility_contradiction`,\n`test_a1_17_subject_entity_preflight`, `test_embed_stability`)\n- [x] Integration tests still pass:\n`test_a4_11_overlap_includes_conflicted_supersedes`,\n`test_a4_status_retraction`, `test_api_contradictions`,\n`test_storage_bulk_endpoints` (53/53)\n- [x] Ruff lint + format clean on the touched files\n- [x] mypy clean on `core-api` (single pre-existing `config.py` croniter\nstub error confirmed on `main` before this PR)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: ran-taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f26e748449a9717d1bfd19f48aff7b52c54e69d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/f26e748449a9717d1bfd19f48aff7b52c54e69d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/2c8942c0b88039aa6cc7b8990420ea39a3de26c1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqFu5KCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuLUQAAVPsd04TFNOMnROsxzFVLM2\noBE2lCRVnWJkytczHBFqjYQfhU8tn2/ErWmdzMNLOH6Ejr20mA8TOj5zdFHs7OL8\nOSKaKHuFu/KlGta6+YVNy++ybPX1XO+XhiS/P4NPU02DQkAfrOG6hG11adCirWRv\nqCRzKoP6LKOhuz+sBaIxq9/eV8UZ12LeeOc4IBiC3+tPAAQTQ9h9A+36gZfhdjUU\ndBzQVvcW11oarEZIulSRbD7F8q3iRhzBX+fhrLfcmcMjDvm0chXi9FvqkT0rBr9v\nVyBUzF5qkFZ7+qr20M7W/0/Cx2DjzdTxiyK2LCcJHbFVQFm6OSqvZutkqVBm0SjM\nwI+UvSWTeQKfrKLaDS6+42ZqqwiFhrqKNwL7h4A6uWdViVh13hINXG3qDqjlhM0d\nskP2C2KObfaS6afYLWDGwm+4i36kCP6tGSj4c1+laQHQjXy1ay55A4QBAzwAisk6\nSFoWJebchHcwreJ3BYGcXsDwaj706vFISGwPrfzdp6VTojpX3VZgrUrq07EHN9U1\n9+TWeqJ4j5N8hpBSb3q2BibHjEFZ2ESc72U8k3/7NMlghk/NmdQJ80xo2/0YbeKi\nIiAZBuSkPuMaYpcWUw1ntOh+7BtDwBURAdXm8Y2FPmw9rxOBuPDIzHiUt+KJUw/B\nWNc6Kl8qU0DNVbRKQsJj\n=quvO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f26e748449a9717d1bfd19f48aff7b52c54e69d2\nparent b17482d06fdfdea0bf3ea1f497f46b17f5d9767e\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1779887690 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779887690 +0300\n\nperf(contradiction): collapse N+1 status updates into batch_update_status per path (P2) (#236)\n\n## Summary\n\nAudit P2 — the contradiction detector issued up to **3K**\n`update_memory_status` HTTPs per detection cycle (K conflicts × 3 call\nshapes per match), all serial, after the parallel LLM `asyncio.gather`.\nThe `batch_update_status` storage endpoint (widened in #222) was sitting\nwith zero callers. This PR is its first consumer.\n\n## Sites collapsed (9 → 3 batch flushes)\n\n| Path | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Semantic (`_detect`, post-gather loop) | 3 call shapes at lines\n433/446/463 | 1 `batch_update_status` |\n| Path C (`detect_contradictions_by_entities_async`) | 3 call shapes at\nlines 1064/1075/1092 | 1 `batch_update_status` |\n| RDF (`_detect`, `for old in rdf_conflicts`) | 3 call shapes at lines\n300/322/347 | 1 `batch_update_status` |\n\n`_attempt_path_c_retraction`'s two sequential `update_memory_status`\ncalls stay — they're not in a loop, only 2 calls; collapsing costs more\nclarity than it saves.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] New `tests/test_p2_contradiction_batch_status.py` (5 tests) —\nasserts shape directly: exactly one `batch_update_status` per cycle,\nzero per-row `update_memory_status`, correct payload contents per path,\nempty paths skip the HTTP, gather-exception isolation\n- [x] Legacy `mock_sc.update_memory_status.call_args_list` assertions in\n7 test files stay green via\n`tests/_contradiction_batch_compat.install_batch_status_replay_shim` — a\none-line addition per test setup that routes the batch call back to\nper-row mock invocations, sparing ~80 mechanical assertion migrations\n- [x] Full contradiction-related sweep: **144/144** unit tests pass\n(`test_contradiction_*`, `test_a4_*`, `test_p1_contradiction`,\n`test_p2_contradiction_batch_status`, `test_visibility_contradiction`,\n`test_a1_17_subject_entity_preflight`, `test_embed_stability`)\n- [x] Integration tests still pass:\n`test_a4_11_overlap_includes_conflicted_supersedes`,\n`test_a4_status_retraction`, `test_api_contradictions`,\n`test_storage_bulk_endpoints` (53/53)\n- [x] Ruff lint + format clean on the touched files\n- [x] mypy clean on `core-api` (single pre-existing `config.py` croniter\nstub error confirmed on `main` before this PR)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: ran-taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-27T13:14:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2c8942c0b88039aa6cc7b8990420ea39a3de26c1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2c8942c0b88039aa6cc7b8990420ea39a3de26c1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2c8942c0b88039aa6cc7b8990420ea39a3de26c1/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b17482d06fdfdea0bf3ea1f497f46b17f5d9767e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b17482d06fdfdea0bf3ea1f497f46b17f5d9767e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b17482d06fdfdea0bf3ea1f497f46b17f5d9767e"}]},{"sha":"b17482d06fdfdea0bf3ea1f497f46b17f5d9767e","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGIxNzQ4MmQwNmZkZmRlYTBiZjNlYTFmNDk3ZjQ2YjE3ZjVkOTc2N2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-05-27T11:17:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-27T11:17:41Z"},"message":"feat(lifecycle): add insights daily cron (#238)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds a sixth lifecycle cron — `lifecycle-insights` — that fans out a\ndaily `generate_insights(focus='discover')` pass per active org. Mirrors\nthe crystallize / entity-link pattern exactly: dedicated topic,\npublisher, subscriber, adapter method, cron tick, fanout case, and\norg-settings flag.\n\nCloses the gap surfaced when a tenant connected to memclaw.net accrued\nmemories for two days without producing a single `memory_type=insight`\nrow: `core-operations` registered only five lifecycle jobs and the\ninsights service was reachable only via the on-demand MCP/REST surface —\nno scheduler called it.\n\n## Behavior\n\n- **Opt-in** — new org setting `insights.auto_insights_enabled` defaults\nto **False** (sibling of `auto_crystallize_enabled` /\n`auto_entity_linking_enabled` but with the inverse default). The\nreflection LLM call is expensive and not universally useful, so\noperators flip the flag explicitly per tenant.\n- **Activity gate** — even on enabled tenants the consumer\nshort-circuits when no non-insight memories have been written since the\nmost-recent insight memory in scope. Two cheap `select max(created_at)`\nqueries; saves the LLM round-trip when the corpus hasn't grown.\n- **Dedup window** — inherits the same `_PIPELINE_DEDUP_WINDOW_HOURS=23`\ngate as crystallize / entity-link.\n- **Scope** — `fleet` when a `fleet_id` is supplied, otherwise `all`.\nStats key is `insights_created` on the `lifecycle_audit` row.\n\n## Changes\n\n13 files, +224/-0:\n\n- `common/events/topics.py` — new `Lifecycle.INSIGHTS_REQUESTED` topic.\n- `common/events/lifecycle_publishers.py` + `__init__.py` —\n`publish_insights_request` reusing `LifecycleArchiveRequest`.\n- `common/events/lifecycle_handlers.py` — `insights` method on\n`PipelineStorageAdapter` Protocol + `insights_op` + third\n`bus.subscribe` in `register_pipeline_consumers`.\n- `core-api/src/core_api/services/lifecycle_audit.py` — `insights()`\nadapter on `_CoreApiLifecycleAdapter` with the two gates; single session\ncovers gate + `generate_insights` + explicit commit (mirrors\n`entity_link`).\n- `core-api/src/core_api/services/organization_settings.py` —\n`\"insights\"` defaults section, `auto_insights_enabled` property (default\nFalse), validator entry.\n- `core-api/src/core_api/routes/lifecycle.py` — `\"insights\"` added to\n`_ACTION_PUBLISHERS`.\n- `core-operations/{config,tasks,app}.py` —\n`lifecycle_insights_interval_seconds` (24h default),\n`run_insights_tick`, `scheduler.register(\"lifecycle-insights\", ...)`.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit: `tests/test_lifecycle_handlers.py` — subscriber happy path +\ndedup-gate skip (2 new tests + Fake adapter extended).\n- [x] Unit: `tests/test_lifecycle_automation.py` — `INSIGHTS_REQUESTED`\ntopic-string + StrEnum format assertions.\n- [x] Unit: `core-operations/tests/test_tasks.py` — cron tick hits\n`/admin/lifecycle/fanout/insights`.\n- [x] Full test suite — 2435 passed, 3 skipped, 1 xfailed, 3 xpassed\nlocally. No regressions.\n- [x] ruff check + format clean on all touched files.\n- [x] mypy clean on core-api/src (161 source files).\n- [x] **Wet test on local stack (dev-71cebd tenant, 1025 active\nmemories)**:\n- Phase 1 — flag OFF (default): fanout fired, audit row `success`,\n`stats={\"insights_created\":0}`, no insight memories created. Gate 1\nconfirmed.\n- Phase 2 — flag ON: fanout fired, **7 insight memories persisted** in\n5s, audit `success`, `stats={\"insights_created\":7}`. Adapter end-to-end\nconfirmed.\n- Phase 3 — re-fire with no new non-insight writes: audit `success` in\n52ms, `stats={\"insights_created\":0}`, insight count unchanged at 7.\nActivity gate confirmed.\n\n## Deploy notes\n\n- No schema migration — org settings live in the existing\n`organization_settings.settings` JSONB column under a new top-level\n`\"insights\"` key.\n- Deploy `core-api` before `core-operations` so the new\n`/admin/lifecycle/fanout/insights` action exists before any cron tick\nreaches it; otherwise the cron would 404 and retry next interval (no\ndata loss, just noise).\n- To enable on an existing tenant: `UPDATE organization_settings SET\nsettings = jsonb_set(settings, '{insights,auto_insights_enabled}',\n'true'::jsonb, true) WHERE org_id = '<tenant>';` (or via whatever\nsettings admin UI is in use).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"48e2db5b844563030ec60c7728cfd8fd839d5a5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/48e2db5b844563030ec60c7728cfd8fd839d5a5a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/b17482d06fdfdea0bf3ea1f497f46b17f5d9767e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqFtLVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9lEQAC89dDQHoYi0FutVI8AhvMxp\nG9/e3ezMWNZ/2NpX5WCZ//p7Imly86Pd0SFQ4TwX6HkQExwb+Lij1xS/YByrsiZ7\nw/SUgTFEFYUfE6xkidglTXXNstIamU72G9g59wPuztyvaS944kNcwU2n9Rh9g2wX\n+JuIcKVG60/xG9VTijxSgSZIx62aVKFhZTZg3e3iRWDt3GfT4sC+jsYT9puEFwa+\nuHXTXiA1YwVI64+n6+MlTKYj62E+SIxfGQgFp5IWeW5FhpYoPbRzxz8t+9vn2B7A\nJ4rsYgwVpUgNWghzACDiOWU7akKXdQBxTPEOhE5h6TXV5FK7+sSKfRogadDI58vv\nJPm81BySNW3fT6j1rdCn695lf9J8H7+nDXQZAntvQxxvcTU9jLqWAfEH9xwf6i8k\n3V4sarMMK1RuLIVACiQftM74p8pRIm8TtvMP/f0v6KU0xHQyMwh+WHEOUtbojpXP\n0p3HW5uOe9ZA5HGC8j+5OkdoAZjItOGGWo9hM99s0tZXMBJ9SJuguQcU4L0uoCYr\niIS0p5nmgn0XZlDPkMgYddHFew/elphPYbAgAX6ijbNn46AS/oBItNLR1fzKW5q8\nSxJYw9dm3vpnGeh25sKzb8q4Ktz+sHMD7qesoDgA3X6KeBOHXKqVJ304I6k5vs36\nykaddi2OdCJTBvwMrTuk\n=SlG3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 48e2db5b844563030ec60c7728cfd8fd839d5a5a\nparent 5ccdd00c6ac5732bfd9e29ac3c32fbd74814b97a\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1779880661 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779880661 +0300\n\nfeat(lifecycle): add insights daily cron (#238)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds a sixth lifecycle cron — `lifecycle-insights` — that fans out a\ndaily `generate_insights(focus='discover')` pass per active org. Mirrors\nthe crystallize / entity-link pattern exactly: dedicated topic,\npublisher, subscriber, adapter method, cron tick, fanout case, and\norg-settings flag.\n\nCloses the gap surfaced when a tenant connected to memclaw.net accrued\nmemories for two days without producing a single `memory_type=insight`\nrow: `core-operations` registered only five lifecycle jobs and the\ninsights service was reachable only via the on-demand MCP/REST surface —\nno scheduler called it.\n\n## Behavior\n\n- **Opt-in** — new org setting `insights.auto_insights_enabled` defaults\nto **False** (sibling of `auto_crystallize_enabled` /\n`auto_entity_linking_enabled` but with the inverse default). The\nreflection LLM call is expensive and not universally useful, so\noperators flip the flag explicitly per tenant.\n- **Activity gate** — even on enabled tenants the consumer\nshort-circuits when no non-insight memories have been written since the\nmost-recent insight memory in scope. Two cheap `select max(created_at)`\nqueries; saves the LLM round-trip when the corpus hasn't grown.\n- **Dedup window** — inherits the same `_PIPELINE_DEDUP_WINDOW_HOURS=23`\ngate as crystallize / entity-link.\n- **Scope** — `fleet` when a `fleet_id` is supplied, otherwise `all`.\nStats key is `insights_created` on the `lifecycle_audit` row.\n\n## Changes\n\n13 files, +224/-0:\n\n- `common/events/topics.py` — new `Lifecycle.INSIGHTS_REQUESTED` topic.\n- `common/events/lifecycle_publishers.py` + `__init__.py` —\n`publish_insights_request` reusing `LifecycleArchiveRequest`.\n- `common/events/lifecycle_handlers.py` — `insights` method on\n`PipelineStorageAdapter` Protocol + `insights_op` + third\n`bus.subscribe` in `register_pipeline_consumers`.\n- `core-api/src/core_api/services/lifecycle_audit.py` — `insights()`\nadapter on `_CoreApiLifecycleAdapter` with the two gates; single session\ncovers gate + `generate_insights` + explicit commit (mirrors\n`entity_link`).\n- `core-api/src/core_api/services/organization_settings.py` —\n`\"insights\"` defaults section, `auto_insights_enabled` property (default\nFalse), validator entry.\n- `core-api/src/core_api/routes/lifecycle.py` — `\"insights\"` added to\n`_ACTION_PUBLISHERS`.\n- `core-operations/{config,tasks,app}.py` —\n`lifecycle_insights_interval_seconds` (24h default),\n`run_insights_tick`, `scheduler.register(\"lifecycle-insights\", ...)`.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit: `tests/test_lifecycle_handlers.py` — subscriber happy path +\ndedup-gate skip (2 new tests + Fake adapter extended).\n- [x] Unit: `tests/test_lifecycle_automation.py` — `INSIGHTS_REQUESTED`\ntopic-string + StrEnum format assertions.\n- [x] Unit: `core-operations/tests/test_tasks.py` — cron tick hits\n`/admin/lifecycle/fanout/insights`.\n- [x] Full test suite — 2435 passed, 3 skipped, 1 xfailed, 3 xpassed\nlocally. No regressions.\n- [x] ruff check + format clean on all touched files.\n- [x] mypy clean on core-api/src (161 source files).\n- [x] **Wet test on local stack (dev-71cebd tenant, 1025 active\nmemories)**:\n- Phase 1 — flag OFF (default): fanout fired, audit row `success`,\n`stats={\"insights_created\":0}`, no insight memories created. Gate 1\nconfirmed.\n- Phase 2 — flag ON: fanout fired, **7 insight memories persisted** in\n5s, audit `success`, `stats={\"insights_created\":7}`. Adapter end-to-end\nconfirmed.\n- Phase 3 — re-fire with no new non-insight writes: audit `success` in\n52ms, `stats={\"insights_created\":0}`, insight count unchanged at 7.\nActivity gate confirmed.\n\n## Deploy notes\n\n- No schema migration — org settings live in the existing\n`organization_settings.settings` JSONB column under a new top-level\n`\"insights\"` key.\n- Deploy `core-api` before `core-operations` so the new\n`/admin/lifecycle/fanout/insights` action exists before any cron tick\nreaches it; otherwise the cron would 404 and retry next interval (no\ndata loss, just noise).\n- To enable on an existing tenant: `UPDATE organization_settings SET\nsettings = jsonb_set(settings, '{insights,auto_insights_enabled}',\n'true'::jsonb, true) WHERE org_id = '<tenant>';` (or via whatever\nsettings admin UI is in use).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-27T11:17:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b17482d06fdfdea0bf3ea1f497f46b17f5d9767e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b17482d06fdfdea0bf3ea1f497f46b17f5d9767e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b17482d06fdfdea0bf3ea1f497f46b17f5d9767e/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5ccdd00c6ac5732bfd9e29ac3c32fbd74814b97a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/5ccdd00c6ac5732bfd9e29ac3c32fbd74814b97a","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/5ccdd00c6ac5732bfd9e29ac3c32fbd74814b97a"}]}]